{"additions":1904,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nPR 3 of 3 for #136 — the final chapters of the user guide. The two remaining stubs (Config Reference, Troubleshooting / FAQ) are replaced in both books, `docs/config.md` is absorbed into the guide and left behind as a thin pointer, and the README's Configuration section shrinks to a minimal example plus links.\n\n## Chapters\n\n**Config Reference** (en + ja) — organized for lookup, everything verified against `assets/default.kdl` and the loader:\n\n- Top-level-at-a-glance table, then one section per node — `theme`, `icons`, `image-preview`, `procs-refresh-interval`, `procs-history`, `github-poll-interval`, `projects-board`, `pages`, `repo-config`, `app` — each with consistent **Form / Default / Merge / Example / Errors** sub-items.\n- Key syntax (named keys and their aliases, `Ctrl+` only), presets and `Nav.*` / `Search.*`, the `\"None\"` unbind.\n- The `page` block: `layout` (sizes, placement rules, inactive panes), both `slot` forms (`then=`+`triggers`, `when`/`then`), `tabs`, `bind`, `pane`/`keys` — with the merge rule stated per element.\n- Pages and panes: per-page tables of every pane, its bindable actions, default keys and meaning. This absorbs docs/config.md's tables and fixes what was stale there: the missing `image-preview` node and the Files view's `OpenDefault` / `OpenWith` actions.\n- Startup errors by category, with real captured messages.\n\n**Troubleshooting / FAQ** (en + ja):\n\n- Reading fail-fast config errors (real captured output; `vig config path` / `--config try.kdl` / `dump` as the iteration loop).\n- `gh` not installed / not authenticated; the Projects `project` scope (`gh auth refresh -s project`, exact notice text).\n- The `⚠ GitHub rate limited` backoff (30s → 10 min cap, `r` retry) and `github-poll-interval`.\n- Nerd Font boxes → `icons \"none\"`; image preview terminal support and `image-preview` modes.\n- Where vig keeps files and how to clear them: config, the GitHub disk cache (`<cache>/vig/v1/<owner>/<repo>/`), the trust store (`$XDG_STATE_HOME/vig/trust.json`).\n- FAQ: read-only guarantees, help overlay as the source of key truth, inactive panes, `vig update`, degrading without `gh` / Docker.\n\nEvery complete example is a ```` ```kdl ```` block loaded by the guide-examples test — **86 verified blocks** across both books now (was 46). `cargo test`: 347 passed. `mise run docs:build` clean; all cross-chapter anchors checked against the built HTML in both books.\n\n## What happened to docs/config.md\n\nIts full content now lives in the guide (mostly the Config Reference; the location/layers/trust material was already in Configuration Basics from PR 2). The file itself stays at its path as a short pointer to the Pages URLs and the in-repo chapter files, so old links keep working. All in-repo references were updated: README (en/ja), guide chapters (introduction, views-projects), the CLAUDE.md new-page checklist, and the code comments in `src/core/config/{merge,repo}.rs`.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- The Pages URLs for the two new chapters go live only after this merges (the docs workflow deploys from `main`).\n- Error messages and cache/trust paths were captured from a real debug build on macOS; Linux differs only by the documented `dirs` conventions (`~/.cache` vs `~/Library/Caches`), which the text states explicitly.\n\nCloses #136\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":14,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T10:14:43Z","deletions":504,"headRefName":"docs/guide-reference","labels":[],"number":146,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLetccA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe changes are documentation-focused and internally consistent, with only minor wording nits identified for the config example comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nCompletes issue #136’s documentation effort by replacing the remaining guide stubs with full **Config Reference** and **Troubleshooting / FAQ** chapters (English + Japanese), while updating existing pointers and slimming the README’s configuration section to route readers into the guide.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add complete Config Reference chapters (en/ja) covering top-level config nodes, `page` block semantics, merge rules, and per-page panes/actions.\n- Add complete Troubleshooting / FAQ chapters (en/ja) with real error/output examples and operational guidance (gh auth, rate limits, cache/trust locations).\n- Convert `docs/config.md` into a thin pointer and update in-repo references (README, docs, and Rust module doc comments) to the new guide locations.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/core/config/repo.rs | Updates module docs to point from `docs/config.md` to the guide’s Configuration Basics chapter. |\r\n| src/core/config/merge.rs | Updates merge-rule docs to point from `docs/config.md` to the guide’s Config Reference chapter. |\r\n| README.md | Shrinks Configuration section to a minimal example and links out to the relevant guide chapters; updates Projects references. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Mirrors README changes for Japanese: minimal config example + guide links; updates Projects references. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Repoints Projects-view documentation links from `docs/config.md` to the guide’s reference/recipes. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/troubleshooting.md | Replaces stub with full Troubleshooting / FAQ content and linked fixes into the Config Reference. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/introduction.md | Updates guide intro to include new chapters (Config Reference + Troubleshooting). |\r\n| docs/guide/src/config-reference.md | Replaces stub with full Config Reference chapter (schema + merge rules + panes/actions + startup errors). |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Japanese Projects-view doc link updates to guide reference/recipes. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/troubleshooting.md | Japanese Troubleshooting / FAQ chapter added (full content replacing stub). |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/introduction.md | Japanese guide intro updated to include the new chapters. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/config-reference.md | Japanese Config Reference chapter added (full content replacing stub). |\r\n| docs/config.md | Collapses old config doc into a pointer to the new guide chapters (keeps old links working). |\r\n| CLAUDE.md | Updates new-page checklist documentation pointers from `docs/config.md` to the guide reference chapters. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 14/14 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T10:18:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"d50f68442281d70323a5ba0c917f9638fc5f7c0f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLewJ8Q","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T10:24:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"0f48317b0ac6ed61898fd1bcda39b0345312727d"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLewMQQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T10:24:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"0f48317b0ac6ed61898fd1bcda39b0345312727d"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLexX_w","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nAt least one internal guide link uses a likely-broken heading anchor (`#-github-rate-limited`) that should be corrected to avoid shipping dead navigation.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**Previously missed (2)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**docs/guide/src/config-reference.md:192**\n* The anchor link to the rate-limit section uses `#-github-rate-limited`, but the actual heading text in `troubleshooting.md` is `## `⚠ GitHub rate limited``; mdBook/GitHub-style slugging typically yields `#github-rate-limited` (no leading `-`), so this link is likely broken.\n```\nbackoff. See [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md#-github-rate-limited)\n```\n**docs/guide/ja/src/config-reference.md:190**\n* The anchor link to the rate-limit section uses `#-github-rate-limited`, but the target heading in `troubleshooting.md` is `## `⚠ GitHub rate limited``; the generated slug is typically `#github-rate-limited` (without the leading `-`), so this link is likely broken.\n```\n[トラブルシューティング](troubleshooting.md#-github-rate-limited)。\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 14/14 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T10:27:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"0f48317b0ac6ed61898fd1bcda39b0345312727d"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T10:40:18Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33383458744/job/99460757114","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-31T10:40:26Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"